// @no-instantiate
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: an arm-valued map that comes back from a CALL, in a program that also
// declares a standalone struct of the arm's exact layout. Twelve lines, no import, no
// generic, no lambda, no `??`, one nesting level.
//
// `vl check` exits 0 with NO diagnostics at all and is the ONLY command that misses it;
// `vl check --codegen` exits 1, `vl check --codegen --no-validate` exits 0, `vl build`
// writes the `.wasm` and exits 1, `vl run` exits 1:
//
//   the emitted module is not valid wasm … type mismatch:
//   expected (ref $type), found (ref $type)
//
// (No byte offset quoted on purpose: it moves with the seed. The two `$type`s are the arm's
//  variant-table heap and the twin's struct-table heap, which `DECISIONS.md` keeps in two
//  namespaces on purpose: "the variant/struct-TABLE seam stays nominal". As with its
//  predecessor the message has no `ref null` in it.)
//
// IT IS THE RESIDUE OF D139, WHICH IT REPLACES AS THE SPECIMEN. D139's own repro is the
// same program with the map bound DIRECTLY at module scope, and it now runs: the D81
// destination-pin pass grew the module-scope run it never had, so `thru(c)` pins
// `c: {[string]: Circle}` onto the top-level binding exactly as it already did onto a
// function-scoped one. Here the binding sits inside `mkm` and reaches `thru` through an
// INFERRED RESULT, and `dstPinSrcIs` does not cross a call it is not the argument of.
//
// SEVEN CONTROLS, all built and RUN against the tree this file ships with — never reasoned:
//
//   delete `type Dot`                              -> LOUD emit reject
//   `type Dot = { q: i32 }` (a non-twin)           -> LOUD emit reject
//   delete `type Shape = Circle | Sq`              -> RUNS
//   annotate `const c: {[string]: Circle}`         -> RUNS
//   annotate `function mkm(): {[string]: Circle}`  -> RUNS
//   bind the map directly (D139's own repro)       -> RUNS  (that row's close)
//   wrap the call site in a function               -> check-clean invalid wasm
//
// THE FIFTH CONTROL IS THE ONE THAT NAMES THE CHANNEL: a declared RESULT annotation makes it
// run, so the deciding information exists and the pin cannot see it. THE SEVENTH IS WHAT
// SEPARATES THIS ROW FROM D139: D139 was storage-class DEPENDENT — its function-scope
// sibling ran — and this one is not. Both scopes are silent, so `scripts/silent-sweep/d139/`'s
// `bind` axis does not discriminate here and the axis that does is the RESULT annotation.
//
// PRE-EXISTING on `54780e0b`, same message at the same offset — not a regression from the
// change this file ships with. Filed as `silent-class-inventory.md` D155.
//
// IT IS THE SPECIMEN. This file is kept byte-for-byte identical to
// `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts`'s `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` below its header, which needs a
// program that type-checks clean and whose module the engine refuses.
//
// WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates), which is the point:
// delete it, graduate a `@run` row, and swap `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` for another live member of
// the class. READ THE NOTE IN `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` BEFORE DOING THAT — including
// what it says about where to look before concluding the class is empty. Three more live
// members are filed with runnable witnesses as D156, D157 and D158.
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
type Dot = { r: i32 }
function thru(x: {[string]: Circle}) { return x }
function mkm() {
  const c = Map()
  c["o"] = { r: 7 }
  return c
}
thru(mkm())
print(7)
